  "entry": "code/index.html",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Open a remote multiscale, multichannel OME-Zarr image from a URL in the browser, then turn channels on and off, recolor them, set contrast, step through Z, and pan or zoom. The README names viewing several pyramidal OME-Zarr images together, such as the outputs of image registration, as vizarr's main use; this run had a single-image store, so that use was not reached. This run covers only the standalone web app; the notebook Python API, the README's second main interface, was out of scope. Data used in the run: public. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
